   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The share of women in the poorest wealth quintile accessing skilled birth assistance</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2018-12-15" value="57.5" year="2018"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-12-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-12-15"></period-end>
     <target value="67">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expected to be achieved by end-2026. The achievement of this target will also be supported by Decree 2025-672 on mandatory health insurance, issued in October 2025 and backed by the Benin Accelerated Economic Transformation and Jobs DPF series. The decree guarantees full or partial premium coverage for the extreme poor and poor, and expands the benefits basket for pregnant women, including antenatal care. Closing period corresponds to Closing Date of Credit C (Cat DDO part).

See DPF2 (P181457) for adjusted indicator proposed to be &quot;Percentage of births attended by skilled health personnel in the twelve communes with the highest poverty rate based on the RSU&quot; with baseline at 74.3 and target at 79.6</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="57.5"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
